(7018433, 1062020, 94265, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dcanossa:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Purple_Girl:</b></div><hr/><i> This could be viewed as a comment on social acceptance norms and the perception of beauty, i.e. the man is walking away from the statue of the very rotund lady, which reflects a lot of the feeling amongst men concerning real women in everyday life, due in part to the standards of beauty put upon us by media. I''m actually bumping my vote up on this one since it made me ponder. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I totally agree with you. It seems like nudity (even partial) is only suitable for trim people. That tells a lot about us as a society, everywhere. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Definitely. I''m disappointed that this didn''t score a bit higher.</td>', 'Originally posted by dcanossa: Originally posted by Purple_Girl: This could be viewed as a comment on social acceptance norms and the perception of beauty, i.e. the man is walking away from the statue of the very rotund lady, which reflects a lot of the feeling amongst men concerning real women in everyday life, due in part to the standards of beauty put upon us by media. I''m actually bumping my vote up on this one since it made me ponder.   I totally agree with you. It seems like nudity (even partial) is only suitable for trim people. That tells a lot about us as a society, everywhere.   Definitely. I''m disappointed that this didn''t score a bit higher.', '2013-04-11 21:52:19.000000', NULL, 0),
